Go 1.18 — math/rand is not auto-seeded (that was introduced in 1.20). Since the test only checks the range, it would pass even with the default seed, but for proper randomness we should seed it. Use `rand.New(rand.NewSource(time.Now().UnixNano()))` or a package-level source. In Go 1.18, the top-level `rand.Intn` uses a global source that is seeded with 1 by default. To make it truly random, seed it in init.

